.TH DANBY-ALTERNATIVEPREDATION 1
.SH NAME
danby-alternativepredation \- predator-prey model with saturating consumption
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/alternativepredation
.SH MODEL
C = aXY/(1+hX);
X' = rX-C;
Y' = cC-dY.
.PP
The handling coefficient h makes consumption saturate as prey become abundant,
instead of increasing without bound as in mass-action predation.  A positive
equilibrium exists when ca>dh; otherwise the display marks the origin.
.SH DISPLAY
The phase portrait exposes the changed nullclines while the time plot makes
the amplitude and phase lag of population cycles explicit.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the phase portrait to set initial populations and the bottom tracks to
set birth, attack, conversion, death, and handling.  Space pauses, period
steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/alternativepredation.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/alternativepredation.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-ecology (1),
.IR numerics (2)
